From 480dce47f61598d8eaebc1c5c98cd1619478a180 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: strata-4gb <strata-4gb@localhost>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:41:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] engine: strata pack --gguf X --out DIR writes the pack
 itself, byte-identical to iq_pack.py

The pack is derived data (dense weights in the engine's layout + tensor index + expert offsets),
so the engine can produce it from a GGUF with no Python, no numpy and no GPU:

    strata pack --gguf model.gguf --out <pack dir> [--compat-bf16]

- include/strata/artifact/pack_build.hpp: header-only port of tools/iq_pack.py's writer --
  the FORM table, the exact/narrow/widen conversions, 64-byte alignment, index.txt v3 rows
  (pool offsets filled in a second pass, like write_index), native_experts.txt v3 with the
  per-role absolute offsets. Quantized sources that need dequantizing report it (the python
  tool stays the fallback for those).
- src/program/generate.cpp: the  subcommand (no GPU touched, no model load)
- serve/prepare.py: prefers , falls back to tools/make_pack.py, then makes
  sure <pack>/tokenizer exists (the engine has no tokenizer; tools/strata_tokenizer.py does)
- serve/server.py: ensure_paths now runs before ensure_pack (the packer needs a resolved exe),
  and slot_save_path is filled when it is still a %placeholder%

Verified:  on Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-IQ3_S produces dense.bin / index.txt /
native_experts.txt byte-identical to the pack tools/iq_pack.py built (cmp, 3/3), and the
portable tree goes from one GGUF path to 'ready: http://127.0.0.1:13502/v1' with the engine
writing the pack.
